From: Stained Glass OS <dev@stained-glass.example>
Subject: msi: a custom action that raises any exception fails like a page fault

The custom action server caught only page faults. A C++ exception escaping
a DLL custom action (Foxit PDF Reader's installer) started the debugger,
whose crash dialog left a silent install waiting forever. Any exception is
now caught and logged and the install goes on, as a page fault already did.

Gate: test/msica-gate.sh.
---
--- a/dlls/msi/custom.c
+++ b/dlls/msi/custom.c
@@ -554,9 +554,13 @@
         {
             r = custom_proc_wrapper( fn, hPackage );
         }
-        __EXCEPT_PAGE_FAULT
+        __EXCEPT_ALL
         {
-            ERR( "Custom action (%s:%s) caused a page fault: %#lx\n",
+            /* Any exception, not only a page fault: a C++ exception escaping
+             * a custom action (Foxit PDF Reader's) otherwise took the whole
+             * custom action server to the debugger, whose crash dialog left
+             * a silent install waiting forever. */
+            ERR( "Custom action (%s:%s) raised exception %#lx\n",
                  debugstr_w(dll), debugstr_a(proc), GetExceptionCode() );
             r = ERROR_SUCCESS;
         }
